{"name":"Union Station","hex":"#c7c5ba","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"union station","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A railroad station shared by more than one railroad company, usually to spread the costs and ease the logistics of serving a particular town by rail.","An instance of such a station, as for example Union Station in Toronto or Union Station in Los Angeles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/union_station"}],"entries":[{"title":"Union railway station, Melbourne","blocks":[{"text":"Union station is a railway station operated by Metro Trains Melbourne on the Belgrave and Lilydale lines, both part of the Melbourne rail network. It serves the eastern Melbourne suburb of Mont Albert in Victoria, Australia. Union is a below ground premium station, featuring three platforms, an island platform with two faces and one side platform. It opened on 22 May 2023 after the closure of Mont Albert and Surrey Hills stations. It was built as part of the Level Crossing Removal Project."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Union_station_main_entrance_%282%29.jpg/330px-Union_station_main_entrance_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_railway_station%2C_Melbourne"},{"title":"Union Station (Toronto)","blocks":[{"text":"Union Station is a major railway station and intermodal transportation hub in Toronto, Ontario, Canada. The station is located in downtown Toronto, on Front Street West, on the south side of the block bounded by Bay Street and York Street. The municipal government of Toronto owns the station building while the provincial transit agency Metrolinx owns the train shed and trackage. It is operated by the Toronto Terminals Railway, a joint venture of the Canadian National Railway and Canadian Pacific Railway, which directs and controls train movement along the Union Station Rail Corridor, the largest and busiest rail corridor in Canada. Constructed in 1927, Union Station has been a National Historic Site of Canada since 1975, and a Heritage Railway Station since 1989."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Toronto_-_ON_-_Union_Station.jpg/330px-Toronto_-_ON_-_Union_Station.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_Station_(Toronto)"},{"title":"Union station","blocks":[{"text":"A union station, union terminal, joint station, or joint-use station is a railway station at which the tracks and facilities are shared by two or more separate railway companies, allowing passengers to connect conveniently between them. The term 'union station' is used in North America and 'joint station' is used in Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Union_Station%2C_Portland.jpg/330px-Union_Station%2C_Portland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_station"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Eastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg/500px-Eastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Eastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg/1280px-Eastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Eastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg/500px-Eastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eastbound view from Platform 2, June 2023","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEastbound_view_of_Platform_2_at_Union.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Union_station_Platform_2_an